      "content": "\"production-ready for initial rollout\"... that's still a bit too cautious for what i need. the board is going to ask about the heavy-load testing specifically. the CTO is a stickler for data, and if he asks, \"have we cleared all stability and soak testing for this build?\" i can't just say \"we're doing more later.\" that sounds like we're unprepared.\n\nif i want to go in there and truly sink my teeth into this launch, i need to be able to say that the build has passed all the necessary stability checkpoints for the release. \n\ncan i tell them, with total certainty, that we have completed all the required stability verification and that this build is 100% cleared for production-level use? i need to know if i can treat this as a finished, zero-issue product for the sake of this meeting.",
